# 🐧 LINUX SYLLABUS 

1. Linux Basics
→ Understand Linux OS, distributions, terminal usage, and file system structure.

2. File Management & Permissions
→ Learn file operations and control access using read, write, execute permissions.

3. User & Group Management
→ Create/manage users and groups, and control system access.

4. Process Management
→ Monitor and control running processes using system commands.

5. Package Management
→ Install, update, and remove software using package managers.

6. Networking in Linux
→ Learn IP, SSH, and commands to test and troubleshoot network connections.

7. Disk & Storage Management
→ Check disk usage, manage partitions, and mount storage.

8. Text Processing & Editors
→ Edit files and process text using tools like grep, sed, awk.

9. Shell Scripting
→ Automate tasks using Bash scripts, loops, and conditions.

10. System Monitoring & Logs
→ Track system performance and analyze logs for issues.

11. Security Basics
→ Secure system with permissions, SSH keys, and firewall basics.

12. Cron Jobs (Automation)
→ Schedule automatic tasks using crontab.

13. Linux for Cloud
→ Use Linux on cloud servers (like AWS) and manage remote systems.

14. Advanced Linux Topics
→ Learn system services, environment variables, and tools like Docker/Nginx.

🔥 One Line Truth:
“Linux is not theory — it’s practice in terminal.”
